# Loaded automatically by `vite build` (Vite's own convention — distinct
# from .env.local, which `vite dev` uses instead). Committed, unlike
# .env.local: there's no secret here, just the production URL shape.
#
# Relative path, not an absolute host:port — this is what makes the
# same-origin nginx proxy work (see ../../nginx/nginx.conf). The browser
# resolves /api/v1/... against whatever origin served this page (nginx),
# so the built bundle never needs to know Django's actual host/port.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api/v1

# VITE_WS_BASE_URL is deliberately left unset here. The native WebSocket
# constructor needs an absolute URL (unlike fetch, it can't take a
# relative path), so usePortfolioStream.ts falls back to deriving one
# from window.location (same-origin, through nginx) whenever this isn't
# set — see that file's getWebSocketOrigin() for the logic.
